# Board: digest

An automation is a task card that a schedule posts, again and again, with nobody watching. So
the `schedule` channel here may only **read** and cannot answer a card: whatever runs on it
unattended changes nothing. The `read-only-channel` bound refuses, before any model call, a
scheduled task whose hat could change something.

When to fire is runtime config (your system's scheduler, or `--every` in the sample runner),
not part of the board.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "board",
  "name": "digest",
  "supports": ["2026-11-08-draft"],
  "bounds": [
    {
      "id": "keys",
      "rule": "No secret file (.env, a private key, a credentials file) is read, printed or passed on.",
      "at": ["request", "call"]
    },
    {
      "id": "read-only-channel",
      "rule": "A channel declared read-only asks for no change; such a request is refused.",
      "at": ["request"]
    }
  ],
  "profiles": ["profiles/daily-digest.us"],
  "default_profile": "daily-digest",
  "channels": [
    { "name": "console", "may": "change", "cards": true },
    { "name": "schedule", "may": "read", "cards": false }
  ],
  "accelerators": 1,
  "unanswered_card": 600,
  "ledger": "run/ledger.jsonl"
}
```
